      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two patients with documented Takayasu's arteritis and severe left main coronary lesion were operated on. The first patient was a 17-year-old boy operated with a double saphenous vein coronary artery bypass graft in 1982, the patient survived 12 years but died suddenly due to associated aortic insufficiency. The second case was a 46-year-old female patient who was successfully operated on."},
